  "title": "Cedar Planter Boxes",
  "summary": "A matched pair of 2 ft square raised planters in cedar, with a stained rim and drainage gaps.",
  "difficulty": "beginner",
  "estimatedHours": 3,
  "imageUrl": "/projects/cedar-planter-boxes.jpg",
  "currency": "USD",
  "steps": [
    "Cut twelve 24 in lengths from the cedar: four per box for the sides and two per box for the corner blocks.",
    "Drill 1/4 in drainage holes through the bottom of each side and two in the middle of the base.",
    "Stack the four sides, gluing and screwing the corner blocks, to make a 24 in square box.",
    "Screw the two blocking strips across the underside so the base sits 2 in up off the patio.",
    "Sand the top rim smooth and round over the corners by hand.",
    "Brush on two coats of exterior stain on the outside faces and let dry."
